A detail worth remembering: the Bronze task runs all three Auto Loader feeds in one notebook. We did not create separate Bronze tasks for Sales, Inventory and Returns.
Why did we configure dependencies?
The tasks cannot all run at the same time because some depend on data created by others.

Our dependency structure was:
bronze_ingestion

jdbc_ingestion

These two start independently and can execute in parallel.
sales_silver


master_silver


inventory_silver


returns_silver



Sales, Inventory and Returns depend on Bronze ingestion. Master Silver depends on JDBC ingestion.
gold_dimensions

Depends on master_silver

gold_facts

Waits for all four Silver tasks and gold_dimensions

gold_business

Depends on gold_facts

gold_validation

Runs after gold_business


Why can Bronze and JDBC run in parallel?
They are independent source-ingestion processes.

Bronze ingestion produces the transaction/event data.

JDBC ingestion produces the master data.

Neither needs the other's output to complete its initial ingestion.
Why does Gold Facts wait for all Silver tasks?
Gold facts need the cleaned transaction data and the corresponding dimensions.

For example, Sales Fact uses Sales Silver and needs the relevant product and store dimensions.

If a fact table starts before the necessary Silver or dimension tables are ready, it may fail or produce incomplete output.
Why does Gold Validation run last?
Because we want to validate the final business-ready tables only after all Gold transformations have finished.

It acts as the final quality gate of the workflow.
